## Roothide entitlements

The `roothideEntitlements` constant in `internal/rootless/roothide.go` is
derived from RootHidePatcher's `roothide.entitlements` (GPL-3.0 — format
reference only, see the package doc comment): the four keys are
Apple-defined functional entitlement data (`platform-application`,
`com.apple.private.security.no-sandbox`, and the AppBundles/
AppDataContainers storage grants), not creative expression.

## Omega (jailbreak.party blacklist remover) — MIT

- **Component:** the Omega restore set for the `xkvm device omega`
  command — the exact domains/paths, record modes, skip-setup plists
  (`internal/device/omega_files/`), and the device-link protocol shape
  (mbdb codec + mobilebackup2 restore flow, as driven by
  sparserestore/TrollRestore via pymobiledevice3).
- **Upstream:** https://github.com/jailbreakdotparty/Omega (MIT,
  copyright (c) 2026 jailbreak.party). Ported from Python to Go; the
  payload files are embedded verbatim.
- **Purpose:** clears the app-revoke and certificate-validity databases
  via a partial backup restore. Use at your own risk — make a backup and
  turn off Find My first; xkvm hard-blocks iOS 27 (upstream's own warning:
  restores there can reset data).
